      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn some production scenarios, especially under zero-data-retention requirements, prompt and output data should never reach logs. `Req.__repr__` prints the token ids, the sampling params and the grammar. A couple of places format a `Req` into a log line or error message, including the scheduler watchdog dump and an assertion in the grammar manager.\n\n## Modifications\n\nWhen `SGLANG_REDACT_REQUEST_DATA=1` is set, `Req.__repr__` prints only the rid and the input and output lengths, and the server refuses to start with `--log-requests`, `--crash-dump-folder` or `--log-level debug`. The default is unchanged. Putting the flag in the repr covers every call site with one small change. The PR also adds unit tests and a docs entry.\n\nIf you would prefer this on by default whenever `--log-requests` is off, happy to switch it.\n",
